1269
00:54:20.090 --> 00:54:21.759
[chuckles]

1270
00:54:21.842 --> 00:54:23.385
And you'd rather be out front?

1271
00:54:24.636 --> 00:54:27.222
Maybe you should tell her what you want.

1272
00:54:28.015 --> 00:54:29.516
What. like you do?

1273
00:54:29.600 --> 00:54:31.268
Like everyone else does?

1274
00:54:31.351 --> 00:54:33.437
Benji. I want you to meet
some of the people

1275
00:54:33.520 --> 00:54:35.773
I worked with at Runway
a gazillion years ago.

1276
00:54:35.856 --> 00:54:37.524
This is. um. Nigel Kipling.

1277
00:54:37.608 --> 00:54:39.359
-Nigel.
-Pleasure.

1278
00:54:39.443 --> 00:54:41.487
And that's Andy...

1279
00:54:41.570 --> 00:54:43.030
-something or other.
-Okay. Andy.

1280
00:54:43.113 --> 00:54:45.365
-Sachs.
-Sorry. can't remember. Sachs.

1281
00:54:45.449 --> 00:54:46.450
-Hi. hi.
-[Benji] Andy. Hi.

1282
00:54:46.533 --> 00:54:50.162
Oh. God. That dress... that is po-pow!

1283
00:54:50.245 --> 00:54:51.955
No. I really hate po-pow. No. no. no.

1284
00:54:52.039 --> 00:54:53.624
Sorry. I'm sorry.

1285
00:54:53.707 --> 00:54:56.960
It's very nice. Not couture.
not custom. but it is nice.

1286
00:54:57.669 --> 00:54:58.879
Say. are you the gal

1287
00:54:58.962 --> 00:55:01.590
who wrote that piece
in Runway about my gal. Emily?

1288
00:55:01.673 --> 00:55:03.300
-Yes. I am.
-Oh. my God.

1289
00:55:03.383 --> 00:55:04.384
I gotta thank you.

1290
00:55:04.468 --> 00:55:08.806
-Really?
-That was so intriguing to me.

1291
00:55:08.889 --> 00:55:10.516
The writing?

1292
00:55:10.599 --> 00:55:11.558
Photos.

1293
00:55:11.642 --> 00:55:13.393
-The photos were so good.
-The subject.

1294
00:55:13.477 --> 00:55:14.728
-Right?
-[glass shatters]

1295
00:55:15.521 --> 00:55:17.606
[♪ dramatic music playing]

1296
00:55:17.689 --> 00:55:18.774
[Miranda screams]

1297
00:55:19.650 --> 00:55:21.276
[guests gasping]

1298
00:55:21.360 --> 00:55:22.778
Oh. my God!

1299
00:55:23.695 --> 00:55:25.364
Is there a doctor?

1300
00:55:25.447 --> 00:55:27.199
Dad? Dad?

1301
00:55:28.367 --> 00:55:30.702
-Oh. my God. Dad.
-Irv.

1302
00:55:30.786 --> 00:55:31.995
Dad?

1303
00:55:35.749 --> 00:55:38.085
[♪ somber music playing]

1304
00:56:03.402 --> 00:56:04.695
Got a lot to think about.

1305
00:56:04.778 --> 00:56:06.822
A day like today
really puts things in perspective

1306
00:56:06.905 --> 00:56:09.324
how fast time moves.

1307
00:56:09.408 --> 00:56:11.702
How we gotta focus on what's important.

1308
00:56:11.785 --> 00:56:12.953
And priorities.

1309
00:56:13.036 --> 00:56:15.163
-[Miranda] Mm-hmm.
-My father loved Runway.

1310
00:56:15.247 --> 00:56:17.583
-you know.
-Yes. he did.

1311
00:56:17.666 --> 00:56:19.042
So did your grandfather.

1312
00:56:19.126 --> 00:56:20.127
Yeah.

1313
00:56:20.210 --> 00:56:22.504
He hired me. you know.

1314
00:56:22.588 --> 00:56:26.091
And when he passed everything
over to Irv... [chuckles]

1315
00:56:26.174 --> 00:56:28.176
-Yeah.
-...we were the same age.

1316
00:56:28.260 --> 00:56:30.929
We worked so closely.

1317
00:56:31.013 --> 00:56:32.180
Yeah. Right.

1318
00:56:32.264 --> 00:56:33.265
Now it's me and you.

1319
00:56:34.516 --> 00:56:37.561
And I look forward
to carrying that football

1320
00:56:37.644 --> 00:56:39.062
into the end zone together.

1321
00:56:41.148 --> 00:56:42.274
[sighs]

1322
00:56:42.357 --> 00:56:46.361
The end zone. So beautifully put.

1323
00:56:46.445 --> 00:56:48.447
[mourners chattering]

1324
00:56:56.288 --> 00:56:57.456
Isn't this awful?

1325
00:56:58.999 --> 00:57:00.417
I can't believe this is happening.

1326
00:57:00.500 --> 00:57:01.668
It's terribly sad.

1327
00:57:01.752 --> 00:57:02.878
Yes. it is very sad.

1328
00:57:02.961 --> 00:57:06.089
Somehow. Dolce dressed everyone here.

1329
00:57:06.173 --> 00:57:08.842
This entire funeral is their fall '26.

1330
00:57:08.926 --> 00:57:10.677
I mean. they must've driven
to everyone's houses

1331
00:57:10.761 --> 00:57:12.012
flinging out freebies. no doubt.

1332
00:57:12.095 --> 00:57:15.182
-Bloody Domenico. So sly.
-[chuckles]

1333
00:57:15.265 --> 00:57:16.642
He'll do anything to get back at me

1334
00:57:16.725 --> 00:57:18.685
since I put Kendall in the finale of '24.

1335
00:57:19.686 --> 00:57:21.104
Isn't she the greatest?

1336
00:57:21.188 --> 00:57:23.607
He's been chomping at the bit
for vengeance.

1337
00:57:23.690 --> 00:57:25.192
-[Benji] Yeah. [chuckles]
-Over Kendall.

1338
00:57:25.275 --> 00:57:27.069
I can't believe
there's someone named Candle.

1339
00:57:31.865 --> 00:57:33.784
What's Jay gonna do? Do you know?

1340
00:57:33.867 --> 00:57:35.827
Do we have any idea
what he's gonna do with Runway?

1341
00:57:35.911 --> 00:57:37.913
No. no. I have no idea.

1342
00:57:37.996 --> 00:57:39.998
but. I mean. you've seen the man.

1343
00:57:40.082 --> 00:57:42.084
He's not exactly a fashion icon.

1344
00:57:42.167 --> 00:57:45.629
He's dressed head to toe
in performance synthetics.

1345
00:57:45.712 --> 00:57:46.797
Throw a match at him

1346
00:57:46.880 --> 00:57:48.632
and he'll go up like
a Christmas tree in March.

1347
00:57:49.549 --> 00:57:52.094
We're gonna be okay. right?

1348
00:57:52.177 --> 00:57:53.762
Runway is still valuable. right?

1349
00:57:53.845 --> 00:57:56.056
I mean. even without Irv.
They know that. right?

1350
00:57:57.015 --> 00:57:59.226
Sorry. So aggressively rhetorical.

1351
00:58:00.185 --> 00:58:01.478
You know. I have no idea.

1352
00:58:01.561 --> 00:58:03.522
We're just going to have to soldier on.

1353
00:58:04.398 --> 00:58:05.983
[horns honking]

1354
00:58:07.192 --> 00:58:09.820
[Nigel] Runway Italy
helped establish Milan

1355
00:58:09.903 --> 00:58:12.030
as one of fashion's most important

1356
00:58:12.114 --> 00:58:13.907
bases of operation.

1357
00:58:13.991 --> 00:58:18.495
which is why we can own this

1358
00:58:18.578 --> 00:58:20.455
the Brera Academy.

1359
00:58:20.539 --> 00:58:21.957
We're going to have a custom runway

1360
00:58:22.040 --> 00:58:23.875
that will be for fashion

1361
00:58:23.959 --> 00:58:25.377
as well as musical acts.

1362
00:58:25.460 --> 00:58:26.962
The whole evening is going to kick off

1363
00:58:27.045 --> 00:58:29.798
with one of Miranda's trademark speeches.

1364
00:58:29.881 --> 00:58:31.758
This one will be about the intermingling

1365
00:58:31.842 --> 00:58:34.261
of Runway and Italian couture.

1366
00:58:34.344 --> 00:58:35.971
I'm almost finished
with the speech. by the way.

1367
00:58:36.054 --> 00:58:39.349
It will be in your inbox
by the end of the week. Yes. Marta?

1368
00:58:39.433 --> 00:58:41.476
Yeah. this thing
with Irv dying and all that.

1369
00:58:41.560 --> 00:58:43.020
when do we find out if things
are changing around here?

1370
00:58:43.103 --> 00:58:44.563
Yeah. what's Jay's plan for the magazine?

1371
00:58:44.646 --> 00:58:45.605
Is he taking over?

1372
00:58:45.689 --> 00:58:47.232
I mean. does he even like fashion?

1373
00:58:47.315 --> 00:58:48.316
I mean. he wears Drakkar Noir.

1374
00:58:48.400 --> 00:58:49.693
-No. he doesn't.
-Oh. my God.

1375
00:58:49.776 --> 00:58:52.070
I'd like to talk about the looks

1376
00:58:52.154 --> 00:58:56.408
that we're going to feature
in the Brera Academy show.

1377
00:58:56.491 --> 00:58:59.369
Some of the bodies
are very interesting. very...

1378
00:59:00.954 --> 00:59:02.831
body... negative.

1379
00:59:02.914 --> 00:59:04.041
[clears throat]

1380
00:59:04.124 --> 00:59:09.212
No. don't tell me.
I know this. Body positive.

1381
00:59:11.214 --> 00:59:14.259
[sighs] But why. really?
When you think a--

1382
00:59:14.342 --> 00:59:15.677
[Dirk] Oh. my God. He's here.

1383
00:59:15.761 --> 00:59:16.887
[Amari gasps]

1384
00:59:16.970 --> 00:59:19.264
[staff member 1] Yeah.
that's. like. our new owner.

1385
00:59:29.775 --> 00:59:31.359
[♪ tense music playing]

1386
00:59:33.320 --> 00:59:35.197
Always loved your office.

1387
00:59:35.280 --> 00:59:37.032
Can't get views like this anymore.

1388
00:59:37.115 --> 00:59:37.949
[Miranda] Mmm.

1389
00:59:38.033 --> 00:59:41.411
And the size. I mean. wow.

1390
00:59:41.495 --> 00:59:43.747
[Miranda] I remember
you coming to the offices

1391
00:59:43.830 --> 00:59:45.624
as a kid with your father

1392
00:59:46.792 --> 00:59:48.710
and your little lacrosse stick.

1393
00:59:48.794 --> 00:59:51.296
tossing that ball up all around.

1394
00:59:51.379 --> 00:59:52.839
I broke a vase.

1395
00:59:52.923 --> 00:59:55.133
Did you? I don't remember.

1396
00:59:55.217 --> 00:59:57.177
Anyway. sorry it took me a while

1397
00:59:57.260 --> 01:00:00.263
to stop by or call you back.

1398
01:00:00.347 --> 01:00:01.723
We barely noticed.

1399
01:00:01.807 --> 01:00:04.601
But now I'm ready to get ducks in rows.

1400
01:00:04.684 --> 01:00:09.106
kick some concepts around
with you. check boxes. Lunch?

1401
01:00:09.189 --> 01:00:11.983
-Now?
-Bad time? You slammed?

1402
01:00:12.067 --> 01:00:13.276
No. not at all.

1403
01:00:13.360 --> 01:00:15.862
I'll just get someone
to make a reservation at--

1404
01:00:15.946 --> 01:00:17.072
Oh. cafeteria's fine.

1405
01:00:17.155 --> 01:00:20.033
I have a couple calls
that I should return anyway.

1406
01:00:20.117 --> 01:00:22.994
Um. I will see you there in ten.

1407
01:00:28.333 --> 01:00:29.668
Amari?

1408
01:00:31.336 --> 01:00:32.170
Yes?

1409
01:00:32.254 --> 01:00:34.131
We have a cafeteria?

1410
01:00:34.214 --> 01:00:36.133
-Oh. yes.
-Really?

1411
01:00:39.010 --> 01:00:40.011
[phone chimes]

1412
01:00:42.430 --> 01:00:43.640
Cafeteria?

1413
01:00:45.100 --> 01:00:47.602
She's never even been to that floor.

1414
01:00:47.686 --> 01:00:48.979
[elevator bell dings]

1415
01:00:51.940 --> 01:00:52.941
It's frozen again.

1416
01:00:53.024 --> 01:00:54.359
[staff chattering]

1417
01:00:54.442 --> 01:00:55.986
Be back in 20 minutes.

1418
01:00:56.069 --> 01:00:57.571
[chattering stops]

1419
01:00:59.948 --> 01:01:02.200
Hey. What's good here?

1420
01:01:02.701 --> 01:01:03.618
Um...

1421
01:01:03.702 --> 01:01:04.536
All the...

1422
01:01:07.122 --> 01:01:07.956
things.

1423
01:01:08.039 --> 01:01:09.040
You know what?

1424
01:01:09.124 --> 01:01:10.375
Before we eat.

1425
01:01:10.458 --> 01:01:12.419
why don't I introduce you
to some of the guys.

1426
01:01:12.502 --> 01:01:14.838
People. Some of the people.

1427
01:01:14.921 --> 01:01:18.091
Didn't mean to. uh. spring all
these folks on you at once.

1428
01:01:18.175 --> 01:01:19.301
And yet...

1429
01:01:19.384 --> 01:01:22.053
These are just some
consultants that I brought in

1430
01:01:22.137 --> 01:01:23.430
for the restructure.

1431
01:01:23.513 --> 01:01:27.559
The best guys. People. the best people.

1432
01:01:27.642 --> 01:01:29.978
They'll be weighing in on
our organizational alignment.

1433
01:01:30.061 --> 01:01:33.106
operational strategy.
financial architecture.

1434
01:01:33.190 --> 01:01:37.652
digital transformation.
user experience. everything.

1435
01:01:38.278 --> 01:01:39.279
Everything.

1436
01:01:39.362 --> 01:01:41.198
Sandeep. you wanna fill Ms. Priestly in

1437
01:01:41.281 --> 01:01:42.532
on our concepts?

1438
01:01:42.616 --> 01:01:46.286
Absolutely. Sandeep Kapoor.
Harvard MBA. Not important.

1439
01:01:46.369 --> 01:01:49.164
You know. at our offices.
we call you "Miranda Beastly"

1440
01:01:49.247 --> 01:01:51.124
'cause you're a beast in the game.

1441
01:01:51.208 --> 01:01:53.043
And unfortunately.
right now what's happening is

1442
01:01:53.126 --> 01:01:54.461
that beast is leashed.

1443
01:01:54.544 --> 01:01:57.839
And we need to let that
beast free. Let it roam.

1444
01:01:58.506 --> 01:02:00.467
Ugh. Undertakers.

1445
01:02:01.384 --> 01:02:03.929
No. what? Management consultants.

1446
01:02:04.012 --> 01:02:05.096
Like I said.

1447
01:02:05.180 --> 01:02:06.514
[Nigel] McKinsey to my eye.

1448
01:02:06.598 --> 01:02:07.933
[Andy] Pfft. Cute.

1449
01:02:09.142 --> 01:02:10.727
[whispers] Wish I could hear
what they were saying.

1450
01:02:10.810 --> 01:02:12.020
-I know.
-[Andy sighs]

1451
01:02:12.103 --> 01:02:13.355
Anyone want Froyo?

1452
01:02:14.397 --> 01:02:17.442
-What?
-What? Best thing here.

1453
01:02:17.525 --> 01:02:19.027
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1454
01:02:21.404 --> 01:02:23.573
I worry about this generation of kids.

1455
01:02:23.657 --> 01:02:25.492
It's a national emergency.

1456
01:02:30.747 --> 01:02:32.749
It went on for an hour.

1457
01:02:32.832 --> 01:02:35.919
Miranda in the middle
of that circle of suits.

1458
01:02:36.002 --> 01:02:37.587
I have no idea what was agreed to.

1459
01:02:37.671 --> 01:02:38.713
They're gonna cut Features first.

1460
01:02:38.797 --> 01:02:39.923
They always cut the writing first.

1461
01:02:40.006 --> 01:02:41.925
Look. look... [sighs]

1462
01:02:42.008 --> 01:02:44.261
...Miranda is resourceful. all right?

1463
01:02:44.344 --> 01:02:46.221
Whatever this new situation is.
she'll find a way.

1464
01:02:46.304 --> 01:02:48.098
Trust me. [scoffing]
She is always ten steps ahead.

1465
01:02:48.181 --> 01:02:49.474
Well. it's just. you know.
this whole thing

1466
01:02:49.557 --> 01:02:50.725
of having an actual job.

1467
01:02:50.809 --> 01:02:53.853
it's been. like. great. you know?

1468
01:02:53.937 --> 01:02:55.355
Yeah. I know.

1469
01:02:55.438 --> 01:02:56.356
-Hi. hi.
-[coworker] Oh. boy.

1470
01:02:56.439 --> 01:02:57.524
I need to talk to you right now.

1471
01:02:57.607 --> 01:02:59.734
Okay. Okay. Excuse me. please. What?

1472
01:02:59.818 --> 01:03:00.902
Okay.

1473
01:03:00.986 --> 01:03:02.654
You know you said
that you wanted to know about

1474
01:03:02.737 --> 01:03:03.947
what Miranda and Jay were talking about

1475
01:03:04.030 --> 01:03:04.906
in the cafeteria.

1476
01:03:04.990 --> 01:03:05.991
Yeah.

1477
01:03:06.074 --> 01:03:07.158
So ...

1478
01:03:07.701 --> 01:03:08.535
What is that?

1479
01:03:08.618 --> 01:03:09.744
When I was getting Froyo.

1480
01:03:09.828 --> 01:03:11.121
I dropped my spoon on the floor.

1481
01:03:11.204 --> 01:03:12.414
and I put my phone under her chair.

1482
01:03:12.497 --> 01:03:15.792
and it was recording the whole time.

1483
01:03:15.875 --> 01:03:17.085
[♪ mischievous music playing]

1484
01:03:17.168 --> 01:03:18.712
Jin!

1485
01:03:18.795 --> 01:03:22.549
-Yeah. Yup. yup. yup. yup.
-What? You are such a badass!

1486
01:03:22.632 --> 01:03:23.717
Yeah. I know.

1487
01:03:24.884 --> 01:03:26.052
[Jay] We took a look at your budget

1488
01:03:26.136 --> 01:03:29.347
and have some immediate
ideas for scale-downs.

1489
01:03:29.431 --> 01:03:32.434
Show the markets that we are
ready to crank that EBITDA.

1490
01:03:32.517 --> 01:03:33.893
I'm just gonna...

1491
01:03:35.937 --> 01:03:37.522
[exhales deeply]

1492
01:03:37.605 --> 01:03:38.982
You don't wanna know.

1493
01:03:39.065 --> 01:03:40.859
Then don't tell me.

1494
01:03:40.942 --> 01:03:42.736
Oh... Oh.

1495
01:03:44.154 --> 01:03:47.866
I was kidding. What is it? Spill it.

1496
01:03:47.949 --> 01:03:51.578
[whispering] Nigel.
they're cutting everything.

1497
01:03:52.579 --> 01:03:55.206
Features? Reduced to nothing.

1498
01:03:55.290 --> 01:03:56.791
Fashion and Beauty? Decimated.

1499
01:03:56.875 --> 01:03:58.418
Cuts across all departments.

1500
01:03:58.501 --> 01:04:00.503
and anyone who's been here
for longer than five years

1501
01:04:00.587 --> 01:04:02.172
is too expensive and has to go.

1502
01:04:02.255 --> 01:04:03.256
I'm sorry.

1503
01:04:04.674 --> 01:04:05.884
That makes sense.

1504
01:04:05.967 --> 01:04:07.802
-And you know what she said?
-[Nigel] Nope.

1505
01:04:07.886 --> 01:04:09.679
Not a single thing.

1506
01:04:11.848 --> 01:04:12.849
Nigel.

1507
01:04:17.228 --> 01:04:18.438
You know what I think?

1508
01:04:19.522 --> 01:04:24.652
I think I like the bag cross-body.

1509
01:04:28.156 --> 01:04:29.449
That's what I think.

1510
01:04:31.993 --> 01:04:32.994
All right.

1511
01:04:33.661 --> 01:04:34.871
I'll leave you to it.

1512
01:04:44.172 --> 01:04:46.466
[The Marias "No One Noticed" playing]

1513
01:04:46.549 --> 01:04:48.760
I just can't believe
this is happening again.

1514
01:04:48.843 --> 01:04:50.845
Another publication. deleted.

1515
01:04:52.764 --> 01:04:55.725
-I'm sorry. Andy. It sucks.
-Sucks.

1516
01:04:59.938 --> 01:05:02.357
This is where it's all going.
you know? It's...

1517
01:05:02.440 --> 01:05:03.316
It's happening all over.

1518
01:05:03.400 --> 01:05:04.442
It's pharmacies. it's bookstores.

1519
01:05:04.526 --> 01:05:05.652
It's... You name it.

1520
01:05:05.735 --> 01:05:08.238
It's all being downsized.
It's all consolidating.

1521
01:05:08.321 --> 01:05:10.156
No. I just can't accept that. I--

1522
01:05:10.240 --> 01:05:12.951
We... We can't just keep

1523
01:05:13.034 --> 01:05:15.161
sucking the soul out of everything.

1524
01:05:15.245 --> 01:05:18.039
And-and gutting it
and then repackaging it.

1525
01:05:18.123 --> 01:05:20.083
To what end?

1526
01:05:20.166 --> 01:05:23.002
But it's... it's...
We're replacing it. you know?

1527
01:05:23.086 --> 01:05:24.504
I mean. you've basically just described

1528
01:05:24.587 --> 01:05:26.506
what I've done with this building.

1529
01:05:26.589 --> 01:05:29.300
Peter. we're not talking about
you right now. We're talk--

1530
01:05:29.384 --> 01:05:30.510
And also. like.

1531
01:05:30.593 --> 01:05:34.681
journalism matters
more than luxury apartments.

1532
01:05:36.766 --> 01:05:37.851
That's true.

1533
01:05:39.894 --> 01:05:42.105
I'm sorry. I'm just...

1534
01:05:42.188 --> 01:05:44.482
This is such a spectacularly
helpful conversation.

1535
01:05:44.566 --> 01:05:45.400
Thank you.

1536
01:05:45.483 --> 01:05:47.026
-Is it not?
-No.

1537
01:05:53.199 --> 01:05:55.034
I might give you a minute.

1538
01:05:55.118 --> 01:05:56.244
Thanks.

1539
01:06:02.250 --> 01:06:04.502
Hey. I. uh...
I know you gotta go to Italy.

1540
01:06:04.586 --> 01:06:07.088
but if you wanna... [sighs]

1541
01:06:07.172 --> 01:06:09.090
...if you wanna catch up
when you're back. I'd like it.

1542
01:06:10.258 --> 01:06:11.551
But it's up to you.

1543
01:06:15.763 --> 01:06:17.348
[door closes]

1544
01:06:17.432 --> 01:06:19.934
-[horns honking]
-[dogs barking in distance]

1545
01:06:35.909 --> 01:06:36.910
[doorbell chimes]

1546
01:06:38.244 --> 01:06:39.329
Hmm. no.

1547
01:06:40.663 --> 01:06:42.582
-Oh. hi. Stuart.
-Andy.

1548
01:06:42.665 --> 01:06:43.958
-Yes.
-You all right?

1549
01:06:44.042 --> 01:06:46.419
-[stammers] Could I come in?
-Sure. absolutely.

1550
01:06:46.503 --> 01:06:48.463
Um. wasn't expecting you. I suppose.

1551
01:06:48.546 --> 01:06:53.218
Sorry to bother you.
I just. um. need. uh...

1552
01:06:53.301 --> 01:06:55.053
-I think... [inhales deeply]
-Catch your breath maybe.

1553
01:06:55.136 --> 01:06:58.223
Okay. Can't. Um. is she here?

1554
01:06:58.306 --> 01:07:00.183
Yeah. she's. um...

1555
01:07:07.273 --> 01:07:08.441
Brave.

1556
01:07:11.110 --> 01:07:12.862
Ah.

1557
01:07:12.946 --> 01:07:15.073
I don't mean to bother you.
I just need to talk.

1558
01:07:16.199 --> 01:07:18.117
-Talk.
-So. uh. I just need to...

1559
01:07:18.201 --> 01:07:20.370
I just need to... You have a plan. right?

1560
01:07:20.453 --> 01:07:21.996
A secret plan like...

1561
01:07:22.080 --> 01:07:23.498
-like you did--
-I can't hear you.

1562
01:07:23.581 --> 01:07:25.416
Don't you have people you can call?

1563
01:07:25.500 --> 01:07:27.919
I just don't want everyone
to lose their jobs.

1564
01:07:28.002 --> 01:07:29.003
Please. Miranda.

1565
01:07:29.087 --> 01:07:30.755
we have been doing such great work lately.

1566
01:07:30.838 --> 01:07:32.465
We're attracting great writers.

1567
01:07:32.549 --> 01:07:35.009
and people care about the magazine again.

1568
01:07:35.093 --> 01:07:37.428
This job has let me hope again

1569
01:07:37.512 --> 01:07:39.180
for the future. for our future. my future.

1570
01:07:39.264 --> 01:07:41.099
I... I might be able to unfreeze an egg.

1571
01:07:41.182 --> 01:07:42.308
Go home.

1572
01:07:42.392 --> 01:07:44.227
-But I...
-It's late.

1573
01:07:44.310 --> 01:07:47.313
Do not concern yourself with this.

1574
01:07:49.649 --> 01:07:52.193
[quietly] It does not concern you.

1575
01:07:58.157 --> 01:08:00.159
[♪ somber music playing]

1576
01:08:05.123 --> 01:08:06.791
[sighs]

1577
01:08:16.009 --> 01:08:18.469
Hmm. Huh.

1578
01:08:23.558 --> 01:08:24.559
[sighs]

1579
01:08:29.689 --> 01:08:31.691
[keyboard clicking]

1580
01:08:36.613 --> 01:08:38.406
Allora. Milano...

1581
01:08:38.489 --> 01:08:40.783
Nigel. you were saying
that some new directives

1582
01:08:40.867 --> 01:08:42.952
have come in from on high.

1583
01:08:43.995 --> 01:08:45.288
Budget cuts?

1584
01:08:45.371 --> 01:08:48.249
Yes. so. regarding Milan.

1585
01:08:48.333 --> 01:08:50.627
we're cutting John Legend

1586
01:08:50.710 --> 01:08:52.712
because he wants us to ship
his piano there.

1587
01:08:52.795 --> 01:08:53.963
and that's too pricey.

1588
01:08:54.047 --> 01:08:55.673
So. no music.

1589
01:08:56.674 --> 01:08:58.009
Unless we call in a favor.

1590
01:08:58.092 --> 01:08:58.926
[pen clicks]

1591
01:09:00.762 --> 01:09:01.804
No.

1592
01:09:06.059 --> 01:09:08.144
No. She's impossible.

1593
01:09:08.227 --> 01:09:09.729
That cover almost...

1594
01:09:11.105 --> 01:09:12.023
killed me.

1595
01:09:12.106 --> 01:09:17.236
Fine. No music. None at all. No music.

1596
01:09:17.320 --> 01:09:19.238
-Okay. fine. I'll call her.
-Thank you.

1597
01:09:19.322 --> 01:09:23.159
Now. there are a few new
policies across the board.

1598
01:09:23.242 --> 01:09:27.580
The first one is no more
private cars. Uber only.

1599
01:09:27.664 --> 01:09:28.498
[gasps]

1600
01:09:28.581 --> 01:09:31.584
And as for the flights...

1601
01:09:34.462 --> 01:09:35.922
Good afternoon. ladies and gentlemen.

1602
01:09:36.005 --> 01:09:38.675
and welcome aboard
United Airlines Flight 19

1603
01:09:38.758 --> 01:09:40.677
with service to Milan. Italy.

1604
01:09:40.760 --> 01:09:42.345
We'll be coming by with champagne

1605
01:09:42.428 --> 01:09:45.056
for our Polaris business class
passengers shortly.

1606
01:09:45.139 --> 01:09:48.101
If you're seated in economy.
we do have a full flight today

1607
01:09:48.184 --> 01:09:50.728
so please stow your carry-ons
in the overhead compartments

1608
01:09:50.812 --> 01:09:53.564
above you and secure
any personal bags or belongings

1609
01:09:53.648 --> 01:09:55.650
under the seat in front of you.

1610
01:09:55.733 --> 01:09:58.236
I need some... Get me something to drink.

1611
01:10:05.326 --> 01:10:06.869
What is wrong with Miranda?

1612
01:10:06.953 --> 01:10:09.038
Why is she putting up with this?

1613
01:10:09.122 --> 01:10:10.957
Excuse me. Excuse me.

1614
01:10:11.040 --> 01:10:12.583
Uh. Ms. Priestly would like a glass

1615
01:10:12.667 --> 01:10:13.835
of your finest champagne.

1616
01:10:13.918 --> 01:10:16.713
I'm sorry.
That's not served in this cabin.

1617
01:10:16.796 --> 01:10:18.339
They have snack boxes.

1618
01:10:19.090 --> 01:10:20.633
Mmm. Um... [clears throat]

1619
01:10:20.717 --> 01:10:22.218
A snack box perhaps?

1620
01:10:24.303 --> 01:10:26.305
[ Madonna "Vogue" playing]

1621
01:10:28.391 --> 01:10:29.392
♪ Vogue♪

1622
01:10:30.893 --> 01:10:32.895
-[people chattering]
-[photographers clamoring]

1623
01:10:32.979 --> 01:10:34.480
♪Look around♪

1624
01:10:34.564 --> 01:10:36.858
♪Everywhere you turn is heartache

1625
01:10:36.941 --> 01:10:41.279
♪It's everywhere that you go
Look around♪

1626
01:10:41.362 --> 01:10:45.074
♪You try everything you can to escape♪

1627
01:10:45.158 --> 01:10:47.452
♪The pain of life that you know

1628
01:10:47.535 --> 01:10:48.786
♪ Life that you know

1629
01:10:48.870 --> 01:10:52.540
♪When all else fails and you long to be♪

1630
01:10:52.623 --> 01:10:55.877
♪Something better than you are today

1631
01:10:57.503 --> 01:11:00.548
♪I know a place where you can get away♪

1632
01:11:00.631 --> 01:11:02.675
♪It's called a dance floor♪

1633
01:11:02.759 --> 01:11:04.719
And here's what it's for♪

1634
01:11:04.802 --> 01:11:07.180
♪So come on. vogue♪

1635
01:11:07.263 --> 01:11:08.514
♪ Vogue♪

1636
01:11:08.598 --> 01:11:11.976
♪ Let your body move to the music

1637
01:11:12.059 --> 01:11:13.728
♪ Hey. hey. hey

1638
01:11:13.811 --> 01:11:15.563
♪Come on. vogue♪

1639
01:11:15.646 --> 01:11:16.773
♪ Vogue♪

1640
01:11:16.856 --> 01:11:19.650
♪ Let your body go with the flow

1641
01:11:19.734 --> 01:11:22.195
You know you can do it

1642
01:11:34.457 --> 01:11:36.125
Oh. it's so beautiful!

1643
01:11:37.502 --> 01:11:38.628
Just click it.

1644
01:11:40.254 --> 01:11:42.507
-[Benji] Look at that.
-[Emily] What do you think?

1645
01:11:42.590 --> 01:11:46.677
-Oh. yeah. Uh-huh.
-What do you think. Benji?

1646
01:11:46.761 --> 01:11:47.929
[sighs]

1647
01:11:48.012 --> 01:11:49.305
What are you doing?

1648
01:11:49.388 --> 01:11:51.724
Uh... [chuckles] Got hypnotized.

1649
01:11:51.808 --> 01:11:53.643
Benji's buying Emily a very nice necklace.

1650
01:11:53.726 --> 01:11:55.895
Yes. I'm not surprised.

1651
01:11:55.978 --> 01:11:57.897
Last week. he bought her a Monet.

1652
01:11:59.106 --> 01:12:00.024
And a Klimt.

1653
01:12:00.107 --> 01:12:01.984
-Really?
-Oh. yes.

1654
01:12:03.444 --> 01:12:04.278
Come on.

1655
01:12:04.362 --> 01:12:05.947
-What?
-No. I mean. we're gonna--

1656
01:12:06.030 --> 01:12:08.241
Hey. just put it on my tab here.
Just put it on my tab.

1657
01:12:08.324 --> 01:12:09.909
Ah. Pronto?

1658
01:12:09.992 --> 01:12:12.912
Pronto. si. pronto. Um...

1659
01:12:12.995 --> 01:12:16.541
Posso avere il numero di camera...

1660
01:12:17.792 --> 01:12:19.418
Yes. I need a room number.

1661
01:12:19.502 --> 01:12:21.671
Mommy. Roark said he wants

1662
01:12:21.754 --> 01:12:23.297
the eclair from Miss Madeleine.

1663
01:12:23.381 --> 01:12:25.299
but it was my idea to go there.

1664
01:12:25.383 --> 01:12:27.552
Oh. bunny. what do we do
when we get a bit wobbly?

1665
01:12:27.635 --> 01:12:28.886
We... That's right.

1666
01:12:28.970 --> 01:12:31.097
-Breathe in. hold...
-[Bronwyn] Breathe in. hold.

1667
01:12:31.180 --> 01:12:32.014
[inhales deeply]

1668
01:12:32.098 --> 01:12:33.099
...and breathe out.

1669
01:12:33.182 --> 01:12:34.267
And don't forget to do the tappy-tap.

1670
01:12:34.350 --> 01:12:35.977
tappy-tap it all away.

1671
01:12:36.060 --> 01:12:38.062
-There we are. Is that better?
-[Bronwyn] Uh-huh.

1672
01:12:38.145 --> 01:12:40.231
Okay. my love. Now. listen.
can you go get Daddy?

1673
01:12:40.314 --> 01:12:42.066
All right. Love ya.

1674
01:12:42.149 --> 01:12:43.734
-What's up?
-Frank.

1675
01:12:43.818 --> 01:12:45.736
I am in Milan. and as you can see.

1676
01:12:45.820 --> 01:12:47.738
I am stretched thinner
than a pair of Spanx.

1677
01:12:47.822 --> 01:12:49.949
so can you just try parenting?

1678
01:12:50.032 --> 01:12:50.992
Go to Miss Madeleine

1679
01:12:51.075 --> 01:12:52.076
and get them the bloody eclair.

1680
01:12:52.159 --> 01:12:53.494
-I can't do everything.
-You went to Italy.

1681
01:12:53.578 --> 01:12:54.871
I'm here. So...

1682
01:13:03.796 --> 01:13:06.549
[exhales]

1683
01:13:06.632 --> 01:13:10.928
May the bridges I burn light my way.

1684
01:13:11.012 --> 01:13:12.805
-[knocking on door]
-God.

1685
01:13:20.229 --> 01:13:21.314
Hi.

1686
01:13:21.397 --> 01:13:22.773
-[Emily] Andy.
-Do you have a sec?

1687
01:13:22.857 --> 01:13:24.609
-Yes.
-Okay.

1688
01:13:26.652 --> 01:13:27.653
[elevator bell dings]

1689
01:13:29.488 --> 01:13:31.490
[♪ adventurous music playing]

1690
01:13:32.617 --> 01:13:33.701
Okay.

1691
01:13:33.784 --> 01:13:35.202
Well. hello.

1692
01:13:35.286 --> 01:13:37.872
-Hi. [chuckles]
-Look at us. up before dawn.

1693
01:13:37.955 --> 01:13:39.457
I just went for a stroll.
What are you doing?

1694
01:13:39.540 --> 01:13:41.459
-Me? Um...
-Yeah. Where are you going?

1695
01:13:41.542 --> 01:13:42.877
-Como.
-Ah.

1696
01:13:42.960 --> 01:13:44.503
Yeah. I'm doing that story on the winery.

1697
01:13:44.587 --> 01:13:46.088
Oh. Right. right.

1698
01:13:46.172 --> 01:13:47.089
That's cute.

1699
01:13:47.173 --> 01:13:48.174
Dinner tonight?

1700
01:13:48.257 --> 01:13:50.134
I always eat with Tom Ford at Da Giacomo.

1701
01:13:50.217 --> 01:13:51.802
-Little gossip sesh? Hmm?
-Uh-huh. Um.

1702
01:13:51.886 --> 01:13:53.095
Okay. great. I'll text you.

1703
01:13:53.179 --> 01:13:54.180
-Okay.
-Okay.

1704
01:13:57.600 --> 01:13:58.434
Hmm.

1705
01:13:59.894 --> 01:14:00.937
[Emily] Come on.

1706
01:14:01.020 --> 01:14:02.688
Window up. Window up.
Nigel's watching. Nigel.

1707
01:14:02.772 --> 01:14:04.607
What? Bloody hell.

1708
01:14:39.684 --> 01:14:41.519
[laughs]

1709
01:14:42.186 --> 01:14:43.354
There she is.

1710
01:14:43.437 --> 01:14:46.315
Oh. hi. honey. Hi. Don't.

1711
01:14:46.399 --> 01:14:48.192
I'm sorry. I'm just saying. "hello.'

1712
01:14:52.363 --> 01:14:53.906
So how long have you had a place here?

1713
01:14:55.241 --> 01:14:56.367
-Me?
-Mm-hmm.

1714
01:14:56.450 --> 01:14:58.119
-Oh. God. Um...
-[in Italian] Grazie.

1715
01:14:58.202 --> 01:14:59.286
[laughs]

1716
01:14:59.370 --> 01:15:00.496
[in English] I don't know. I don't know.

1717
01:15:00.579 --> 01:15:02.123
He doesn't remember anything.

1718
01:15:02.206 --> 01:15:03.374
-Nothing.
-[chuckles]

1719
01:15:03.457 --> 01:15:04.375
Oh. no. no.

1720
01:15:04.458 --> 01:15:05.793
[in Italian] Non. non per mio. grazie.

1721
01:15:05.876 --> 01:15:07.628
-No. thank you. Massimo.
-[in Italian] Ciao.

1722
01:15:07.712 --> 01:15:08.629
[in English] Not having anything?

1723
01:15:08.713 --> 01:15:10.756
No. I'm not doing water these days.

1724
01:15:10.840 --> 01:15:12.550
Trying to operate at an aqua deficit.

1725
01:15:12.633 --> 01:15:14.135
-It's poison.
-[Emily] Not poison.

1726
01:15:14.218 --> 01:15:15.803
-[Benji] It is poison.
-So. uh.

1727
01:15:16.929 --> 01:15:18.222
do you think we can pull this off?

1728
01:15:18.305 --> 01:15:19.306
[Benji] Depends on what he's asking.

1729
01:15:19.390 --> 01:15:20.725
-Oh. come on. BB.
-What?

1730
01:15:20.808 --> 01:15:22.476
You can persuade anyone
of anything. You know that.

1731
01:15:22.560 --> 01:15:24.979
Well. that's true. I did persuade this one
to go on a date with me.

1732
01:15:25.062 --> 01:15:26.272
To go on a date with you.

1733
01:15:26.355 --> 01:15:27.356
-I know.
-[laughs]

1734
01:15:28.149 --> 01:15:29.775
With all of that ear hair.

1735
01:15:29.859 --> 01:15:31.861
Oh my-- Oh. please.

1736
01:15:31.944 --> 01:15:33.070
It was so awful.

1737
01:15:33.154 --> 01:15:34.780
Andy. if you had seen me
before I met this one.

1738
01:15:34.864 --> 01:15:35.865
I had ear hair.

1739
01:15:35.948 --> 01:15:37.033
[Emily] It was like a jungle in there.

1740
01:15:37.116 --> 01:15:38.034
So much hair growing out of them.

1741
01:15:38.117 --> 01:15:39.243
I had to get him one of the things.

1742
01:15:39.326 --> 01:15:40.995
-The buzzy thing.
-The buzzer. [imitates buzzer]

1743
01:15:41.078 --> 01:15:43.873
Yeah. and then a lawn mower for the rest.

1744
01:15:43.956 --> 01:15:46.167
Can you imagine lawn-mowing my chest?

1745
01:15:46.250 --> 01:15:49.545
I know. I just like him
like a bar of soap.

1746
01:15:49.628 --> 01:15:51.297
That's right. just hairless.

1747
01:15:51.380 --> 01:15:52.381
-[Emily] Oh. there he is.
-Oh.

1748
01:15:52.465 --> 01:15:53.966
What we need to do is get four people on.

1749
01:15:54.050 --> 01:15:55.051
We need to get the accountant.

1750
01:15:55.134 --> 01:15:56.218
we need to get the business manager.

1751
01:15:56.302 --> 01:15:57.511
We need to get everybody's team.

1752
01:15:57.595 --> 01:15:59.221
-Everybody's team.
-Jay!

1753
01:15:59.305 --> 01:16:00.389
Real quick. then.

1754
01:16:00.473 --> 01:16:01.724
You wanna tell me quick?
You can tell me quick.

1755
01:16:01.807 --> 01:16:02.892
[Benji] Jay-Jay!

1756
01:16:02.975 --> 01:16:04.143
You wanna tell me slow.
you can tell me slow.

1757
01:16:04.226 --> 01:16:06.145
-Does he not see us?
-Not at all.

1758
01:16:06.228 --> 01:16:08.230
[bell tolling]

1759
01:16:14.487 --> 01:16:15.488
Oh. there you are.

1760
01:16:15.571 --> 01:16:16.906
-Oh. hi.
-Hi.

1761
01:16:16.989 --> 01:16:18.115
Hey. how was your dinner?

1762
01:16:18.199 --> 01:16:19.909
-Lovely. How was yours?
-Mmm.

1763
01:16:19.992 --> 01:16:21.535
Oh. you know. I just ordered room service.

1764
01:16:21.619 --> 01:16:22.661
-Oh. yeah? Yeah.
-Mm-hmm.

1765
01:16:22.745 --> 01:16:24.413
I love their baccala mantecato here.

1766
01:16:24.497 --> 01:16:25.956
-Yum. It was so good.
-Yeah.

1767
01:16:26.040 --> 01:16:27.291
Yeah. they don't have that here.

1768
01:16:27.374 --> 01:16:29.335
That's a Venetian dish. not milanese.

1769
01:16:29.418 --> 01:16:30.669
-1...
-Tell me the truth.

1770
01:16:30.753 --> 01:16:32.338
-What's going on?
-What? Nigel.

1771
01:16:32.421 --> 01:16:33.422
You're skulking.

1772
01:16:33.506 --> 01:16:35.591
I know a skulk when I see a skulk.

1773
01:16:35.674 --> 01:16:37.259
-Tell me.
-And... She's here.

1774
01:16:37.343 --> 01:16:40.596
-Morning.
-I can't do this clasp.

1775
01:16:41.097 --> 01:16:42.098
Ready?

1776
01:16:45.559 --> 01:16:48.521
[Nigel] Obviously. security
is going to be very intense.

1777
01:16:48.604 --> 01:16:54.527
And we have hired
extensive protezione for the art.

1778
01:16:58.531 --> 01:16:59.615
[in Italian] Grazie.

1779
01:16:59.698 --> 01:17:00.825
[in English] Okay. everybody.

1780
01:17:00.908 --> 01:17:05.079
I'd like to run through
the dinner for the clients.

1781
01:17:05.788 --> 01:17:06.997
the seating.

1782
01:17:07.081 --> 01:17:09.500
so we have a U-shaped table.

1783
01:17:09.583 --> 01:17:11.752
That's the head up there.

1784
01:17:11.836 --> 01:17:14.130
It's going to end around here someplace.

1785
01:17:14.213 --> 01:17:16.423
about 40 people or more...

1786
01:17:16.507 --> 01:17:18.050
And we're going to take the brands.

1787
01:17:18.134 --> 01:17:19.635
and we're going to mix them up...

1788
01:17:19.718 --> 01:17:21.554
Do you know much about The Last Supper?

1789
01:17:21.637 --> 01:17:22.638
[stammers]

1790
01:17:22.721 --> 01:17:23.973
Not as much as I should.

1791
01:17:25.099 --> 01:17:28.602
Painting this particular scene
was nothing new.

1792
01:17:29.854 --> 01:17:32.940
You can find frescoes
of the same subject matter

1793
01:17:33.023 --> 01:17:33.858
all over Europe.

1794
01:17:33.941 --> 01:17:37.486
but in the other versions.

1795
01:17:37.570 --> 01:17:40.906
the man in charge is
usually depicted with a halo.

1796
01:17:43.951 --> 01:17:47.997
People think that it was
da Vinci's way of saying.

1797
01:17:48.080 --> 01:17:51.083
"We are human. No one is perfect."

1798
01:17:52.376 --> 01:17:56.922
Humans are at once glorious and fallible.

1799
01:17:58.132 --> 01:18:01.927
And inevitably we deceive
and betray one another.

1800
01:18:02.011 --> 01:18:03.929
let each other down.

1801
01:18:04.680 --> 01:18:06.849
[sighs]

1802
01:18:06.932 --> 01:18:09.226
It's what we're built to do.

1803
01:18:13.397 --> 01:18:14.398
Would you agree?

1804
01:18:23.324 --> 01:18:25.326
[♪ tense music plays]

1805
01:18:32.750 --> 01:18:34.043
Okay. Yes.

1806
01:18:46.222 --> 01:18:47.389
[laughs]

1807
01:18:47.473 --> 01:18:49.808
What's Andy doing beetling around here?

1808
01:18:50.476 --> 01:18:51.477
[in Italian] Scusa.

1809
01:18:52.937 --> 01:18:54.396
-[in English] Can I help you?
-Miranda knows.

1810
01:18:54.480 --> 01:18:55.689
-What do you mean she knows?
-She knows.

1811
01:18:55.773 --> 01:18:57.942
-How? Did you blab?
-No. but I don't--

1812
01:18:58.025 --> 01:18:59.276
She made it terrifyingly clear to me

1813
01:18:59.360 --> 01:19:00.527
she is aware something is up.

1814
01:19:00.611 --> 01:19:01.779
Oh. for God's sake.

1815
01:19:01.862 --> 01:19:03.364
And I know that we're just
doing this to help her

1816
01:19:03.447 --> 01:19:04.823
but I honestly can't
with the secrets anymore.

1817
01:19:04.907 --> 01:19:06.242
so I think we just...
like. we should tell her.

1818
01:19:06.325 --> 01:19:07.326
-No...
-Yes.

1819
01:19:07.409 --> 01:19:09.161
We will wait until it is done. please.

1820
01:19:09.245 --> 01:19:10.829
[in Italian] Emily. dai.

1821
01:19:10.913 --> 01:19:11.956
Mi dai un momento?

1822
01:19:12.039 --> 01:19:13.540
Perche sei sempre
cosi impaziente. Donatella?

1823
01:19:13.624 --> 01:19:14.667
Per favore!

1824
01:19:14.750 --> 01:19:15.751
[in English] Emily. focus.

1825
01:19:16.877 --> 01:19:17.878
We need to tell Miranda.

1826
01:19:17.962 --> 01:19:19.255
We need to tell her now.

1827
01:19:20.089 --> 01:19:21.757
I feel a little bit sick.

1828
01:19:23.926 --> 01:19:25.094
I'm so nervous I can't breathe.

1829
01:19:25.177 --> 01:19:26.971
-[pants] My neck is hot.
-Oh. my God.

1830
01:19:27.054 --> 01:19:29.348
Just hide a feeling for once. please.

1831
01:19:29.431 --> 01:19:30.683
[knocking on door]

1832
01:19:32.851 --> 01:19:33.686
Oh.

1833
01:19:34.395 --> 01:19:35.271
The Emilys.

1834
01:19:35.354 --> 01:19:36.897
I thought you were Amari.

1835
01:19:36.981 --> 01:19:39.191
Waiting for my Armani.

1836
01:19:39.275 --> 01:19:41.652
Has she been human trafficked?

1837
01:19:41.735 --> 01:19:45.072
Oh. Uh. Jay sprung for the big suite.

1838
01:19:45.155 --> 01:19:46.323
Yeah.

1839
01:19:46.407 --> 01:19:49.618
Well. it's a little snug.
but. you know. I'll manage.

1840
01:19:49.702 --> 01:19:51.120
How can I help you two?

1841
01:19:51.203 --> 01:19:52.621
Um...

1842
01:19:52.705 --> 01:19:55.165
-Okay. Miranda.
-Mm-hmm.

1843
01:19:55.249 --> 01:19:57.334
What Jay wants to do with Runway.

1844
01:19:57.418 --> 01:19:58.585
scaling it so far back that it

1845
01:19:58.669 --> 01:20:00.754
doesn't even resemble what it used to be.

1846
01:20:00.838 --> 01:20:02.172
cutting my department.

1847
01:20:02.256 --> 01:20:03.924
Nigel and most of his department--

1848
01:20:04.008 --> 01:20:05.301
How do you know about that?

1849
01:20:05.384 --> 01:20:08.637
Look. we all know how important

1850
01:20:08.721 --> 01:20:10.180
Runway is and has been.

1851
01:20:10.264 --> 01:20:12.349
Yeah. I mean. Runway is
practically a religion

1852
01:20:12.433 --> 01:20:14.476
and it needs to be protected.

1853
01:20:14.560 --> 01:20:16.228
So I think. you know. the question is.

1854
01:20:16.312 --> 01:20:18.147
who has the means to acquire it?

1855
01:20:18.230 --> 01:20:19.898
Will you two please spit it out already?

1856
01:20:19.982 --> 01:20:20.983
Um... [stammers]

1857
01:20:21.066 --> 01:20:22.067
Benji's buying Runway.

1858
01:20:22.151 --> 01:20:24.528
Benji? Benji Barnes?

1859
01:20:24.611 --> 01:20:27.156
My Benji made Jay Ravitz an offer.

1860
01:20:27.239 --> 01:20:30.659
and Jay readily accepted.

1861
01:20:30.743 --> 01:20:32.202
And you had a part in this?

1862
01:20:32.286 --> 01:20:35.247
Yes. we're doing it
to protect Runway and you.

1863
01:20:35.331 --> 01:20:38.083
You'll be editor-in-chief
for as long as you want to be.

1864
01:20:38.167 --> 01:20:39.877
[stammers] I'm sorry.

1865
01:20:39.960 --> 01:20:43.756
I... I know we've had our differences.

1866
01:20:43.839 --> 01:20:45.007
but I just... I...

1867
01:20:46.383 --> 01:20:47.968
Well. now. I never realized that you

1868
01:20:48.052 --> 01:20:49.803
were capable of this level of betrayal.

1869
01:20:49.887 --> 01:20:51.638
Betrayal? No. Miranda.

1870
01:20:51.722 --> 01:20:54.266
we're preserving Runway for you.

1871
01:20:54.350 --> 01:20:55.476
[Miranda] Oh. no. no. no.

1872
01:20:55.559 --> 01:20:58.604
Miss Emily is not preserving
anything for anybody.

1873
01:20:59.480 --> 01:21:00.647
[stammers] Yes. she is.

1874
01:21:00.731 --> 01:21:01.732
[chuckles] Yes. of course she is.

1875
01:21:01.815 --> 01:21:02.858
Emily.

1876
01:21:05.652 --> 01:21:07.821
Emily. tell her.

1877
01:21:07.905 --> 01:21:09.448
Yeah. Emily.

1878
01:21:10.324 --> 01:21:11.492
Tell her.

1879
01:21:18.957 --> 01:21:20.417
Well. she's right. [sighs]

1880
01:21:23.504 --> 01:21:25.506
Benji's buying Runway for me.

1881
01:21:27.257 --> 01:21:28.509
So that I can run it.

1882
01:21:28.592 --> 01:21:30.094
-What are you talking about?
-[chuckles]

1883
01:21:31.136 --> 01:21:32.262
Look. she's had a long run.

1884
01:21:32.346 --> 01:21:33.722
A historic run.

1885
01:21:34.640 --> 01:21:36.308
But she's exhausted.

1886
01:21:36.392 --> 01:21:39.895
And... And I'm fresher and younger.

1887
01:21:41.355 --> 01:21:43.482
I want to set tastes.
not just cater to them.

1888
01:21:43.565 --> 01:21:44.983
Why would... Why would you do this?

1889
01:21:45.067 --> 01:21:46.568
She knows why.

1890
01:21:46.652 --> 01:21:48.695
[stammers] I have no idea.

1891
01:21:48.779 --> 01:21:50.739
You pushed me out. didn't you?

1892
01:21:50.823 --> 01:21:52.199
I did nothing of the kind.

1893
01:21:52.282 --> 01:21:56.203
You made Dior hire me to get rid of me.

1894
01:21:56.286 --> 01:21:58.372
Why? Why did... Why did you do that?

1895
01:21:59.331 --> 01:22:00.624
[smacks lips. sighs]

1896
01:22:00.707 --> 01:22:02.000
For the same reason

1897
01:22:02.084 --> 01:22:05.045
that you should never
be in charge of Runway. Emily.

1898
01:22:05.129 --> 01:22:08.173
because you are beautiful
and you're intelligent.

1899
01:22:08.257 --> 01:22:09.466
but. no...

1900
01:22:11.260 --> 01:22:13.220
you don't have what it takes.

1901
01:22:14.763 --> 01:22:18.142
I'm sorry. but you're not a visionary.

1902
01:22:20.394 --> 01:22:21.687
You're a vendor.

1903
01:22:23.147 --> 01:22:24.857
You don't know that.

1904
01:22:27.317 --> 01:22:28.735
You don't know the first thing about me.

1905
01:22:28.819 --> 01:22:30.154
You never cared to--

1906
01:22:30.237 --> 01:22:34.366
Oh. I think I do.
and I also think. deep down...

1907
01:22:35.701 --> 01:22:36.702
you know I'm right.

1908
01:22:41.206 --> 01:22:42.207
That's all.

1909
01:22:44.042 --> 01:22:45.294
[breathes shakily]

1910
01:22:47.921 --> 01:22:51.425
Well. Benji's lawyers.
they will be in touch.

1911
01:22:52.301 --> 01:22:53.719
With all the details.

1912
01:22:58.765 --> 01:23:02.936
[stammers] I had no idea.
I'm... I'm so sorry.

1913
01:23:03.020 --> 01:23:05.397
I just felt I had to do something.

1914
01:23:06.690 --> 01:23:08.901
I hope that's not what
you're wearing to the dinner.

1915
01:23:10.944 --> 01:23:12.362
[stammers]

1916
01:23:21.038 --> 01:23:22.456
[sighs]

1917
01:23:25.083 --> 01:23:27.294
[bell tolling]

1918
01:23:31.089 --> 01:23:32.341
[phone buzzes]

1919
01:23:36.386 --> 01:23:38.096
Hey. What's up? How are you?

1920
01:23:38.180 --> 01:23:40.098
Oh. my God. Andy. these pages you sent...

1921
01:23:40.182 --> 01:23:41.266
My boss is freaking out.

1922
01:23:41.350 --> 01:23:42.601
These are perfect.

1923
01:23:42.684 --> 01:23:44.478
Oh. Uh...

1924
01:23:44.561 --> 01:23:46.021
So about that. um. I don't--

1925
01:23:46.104 --> 01:23:47.606
[Talia] There's so much promise here.

1926
01:23:47.689 --> 01:23:49.775
I'm sending you an offer and a contract.

1927
01:23:49.858 --> 01:23:52.528
And. Andy. it's not 50.

1928
01:23:52.611 --> 01:23:53.779
It's not 100.

1929
01:23:54.446 --> 01:23:56.156
It's 350.

1930
01:23:56.240 --> 01:23:57.950
It's three-freaking-fifty.

1931
01:24:01.495 --> 01:24:02.663
-No.
-[Talia] No?

1932
01:24:02.746 --> 01:24:03.747
What do... What do you mean. "no"?

1933
01:24:03.830 --> 01:24:05.874
Don't you mean. like. "hooray"?

1934
01:24:05.958 --> 01:24:07.292
This book.

1935
01:24:07.376 --> 01:24:10.212
it could harm Miranda. I don't...

1936
01:24:10.295 --> 01:24:13.840
[Talia] Which is fine
because she's atrocious.

1937
01:24:13.924 --> 01:24:16.218
It's more complicated than that.

1938
01:24:16.301 --> 01:24:20.097
Okay. Stockholm called.
They want their syndrome back.

1939
01:24:20.180 --> 01:24:23.183
I... [stammers] Can I call you back later?

1940
01:24:23.267 --> 01:24:24.560
Okay. Thanks for letting me know.

1941
01:24:24.643 --> 01:24:25.644
Bye.

1942
01:24:27.229 --> 01:24:29.189
[breathes heavily]

1943
01:24:29.273 --> 01:24:33.402
[Benji laughs] The moon?
We've already been to the moon.

1944
01:24:33.485 --> 01:24:35.612
[Benji] And now. of course.
all the boys wanna go to Mars.

1945
01:24:35.696 --> 01:24:36.613
Fuck Mars.

1946
01:24:36.697 --> 01:24:38.574
Let's go to that big. orange star

1947
01:24:38.657 --> 01:24:39.950
that we call the sun.

1948
01:24:40.033 --> 01:24:41.034
Totally unexplored!

1949
01:24:41.118 --> 01:24:42.661
We've been looking at it for centuries.

1950
01:24:42.744 --> 01:24:43.662
I'm gonna build a little rocket.

1951
01:24:43.745 --> 01:24:44.746
I'm gonna call it The Icarus.

1952
01:24:44.830 --> 01:24:46.331
Icarus did fly too close to the sun.

1953
01:24:46.415 --> 01:24:48.709
-He did fly too close.
-He did. And he fried.

1954
01:24:48.792 --> 01:24:50.460
That's... You're missing the point. honey.

1955
01:24:50.544 --> 01:24:51.628
[Emily] It's like an irony.

1956
01:24:51.712 --> 01:24:52.796
-[Benji] No. it's not ironic.
-What's going on?

1957
01:24:52.879 --> 01:24:53.964
-[Benji] It's...
-Hmm?

1958
01:24:54.047 --> 01:24:55.591
You look like a nervous cat.

1959
01:24:56.883 --> 01:24:58.302
Uh...

1960
01:24:58.385 --> 01:24:59.720
-Compliment?
-No.

1961
01:24:59.803 --> 01:25:01.680
-Hang on a second.
-Oh. Is it... Is it...

1962
01:25:01.763 --> 01:25:03.223
I don't know. I'll go find out.

1963
01:25:03.307 --> 01:25:04.308
So sorry.

1964
01:25:04.391 --> 01:25:05.601
[in Italian] Scusi.

1965
01:25:16.528 --> 01:25:18.363
[in English] I'm ready to make
an announcement.

1966
01:25:18.447 --> 01:25:19.781
Whenever you're ready.

1967
01:25:19.865 --> 01:25:21.074
[Benji] Oh. we're not closed yet.

1968
01:25:21.158 --> 01:25:22.951
Still ironing out some of the details.

1969
01:25:23.619 --> 01:25:25.329
Oh. I see.

1970
01:25:26.830 --> 01:25:27.956
[sighs]

1971
01:25:30.709 --> 01:25:34.296
So generous what you're doing for Emily.

1972
01:25:34.379 --> 01:25:35.380
Oh.

1973
01:25:37.674 --> 01:25:40.886
[chuckles] I know she has many plans.

1974
01:25:40.969 --> 01:25:44.389
But I do hope that some Runway traditions

1975
01:25:44.473 --> 01:25:45.682
are allowed to remain.

1976
01:25:46.808 --> 01:25:47.643
Hmm.

1977
01:25:48.185 --> 01:25:49.645
Who knows?

1978
01:25:49.728 --> 01:25:51.480
Look. the world
is changing so fast sometimes

1979
01:25:51.563 --> 01:25:53.649
that even I can't comprehend it.

1980
01:25:53.732 --> 01:25:55.776
So tradition. well...

1981
01:25:55.859 --> 01:25:58.111
I think a day is coming.
perhaps very soon.

1982
01:25:58.195 --> 01:25:59.446
where. you know.

1983
01:25:59.529 --> 01:26:00.947
Runway won't need models

1984
01:26:01.031 --> 01:26:03.950
or locations or even designers.

1985
01:26:04.034 --> 01:26:06.244
It'll all just. you know. be Al.

1986
01:26:06.328 --> 01:26:07.788
Mmm. Mmm.

1987
01:26:07.871 --> 01:26:11.833
Surely some things will stay the same.

1988
01:26:11.917 --> 01:26:15.504
A commitment to beauty. artistry.

1989
01:26:16.963 --> 01:26:21.551
the best in human achievement. maybe.

1990
01:26:21.635 --> 01:26:22.636
Maybe.

1991
01:26:23.553 --> 01:26:24.554
But...

1992
01:26:26.973 --> 01:26:27.974
look around you.

1993
01:26:29.810 --> 01:26:33.105
We're in an ancient city
that was once part of

1994
01:26:33.188 --> 01:26:35.732
one of the greatest empires
that the world has ever known.

1995
01:26:35.816 --> 01:26:38.527
Now there's just little traces of it left.

1996
01:26:40.278 --> 01:26:41.780
The world is about change.

1997
01:26:41.863 --> 01:26:44.199
That's what human beings don't understand.

1998
01:26:44.282 --> 01:26:46.618
The future just comes
rushing at us like. um...

1999
01:26:47.452 --> 01:26:49.871
well. like the lava of Pompeii.

2000
01:26:52.290 --> 01:26:53.500
Our job is to just let it take

2001
01:26:53.583 --> 01:26:55.794
what it wants to take. you know?

2002
01:26:55.877 --> 01:26:56.712
One day. it's going to come

2003
01:26:56.795 --> 01:26:58.171
and it's going to smother us all.

2004
01:26:58.255 --> 01:27:01.174
[laughs. snorts]

2005
01:27:01.258 --> 01:27:03.260
And maybe that's the way
it has to be. hmm?

2006
01:27:11.476 --> 01:27:12.477
[softly] Maybe.

2007
01:27:16.148 --> 01:27:17.274
Excuse me.

2008
01:27:28.535 --> 01:27:30.537
[♪ pensive music playing]

2009
01:28:12.954 --> 01:28:14.164
-Hey.
-[gasps]

2010
01:28:15.123 --> 01:28:16.416
You made it.

2011
01:28:16.500 --> 01:28:17.667
Yeah. sorry.

2012
01:28:17.751 --> 01:28:19.419
I should know those flights

2013
01:28:19.503 --> 01:28:21.254
from Copenhagen are always delayed.

2014
01:28:21.338 --> 01:28:22.214
[sighs]

2015
01:28:22.297 --> 01:28:23.465
Hey. hey. hey. What's wrong?

2016
01:28:25.967 --> 01:28:28.178
[sighs]

2017
01:28:31.598 --> 01:28:34.851
How will I know when it's time?

2018
01:28:37.938 --> 01:28:39.272
Uh... [sighs]

2019
01:28:40.565 --> 01:28:41.817
You'll know.

2020
01:28:46.988 --> 01:28:48.198
And if I leave?

2021
01:28:49.115 --> 01:28:50.116
What happens?

2022
01:28:52.536 --> 01:28:53.537
What will I have?

2023
01:28:54.746 --> 01:28:56.206
What do you have?

2024
01:28:57.833 --> 01:28:59.042
Well. you have the twins.

2025
01:29:00.460 --> 01:29:02.546
You've got one very badly behaved dog.

2026
01:29:02.629 --> 01:29:04.130
Gotta talk to you about him.

2027
01:29:04.214 --> 01:29:05.215
And. um...

2028
01:29:08.510 --> 01:29:09.970
you have me.

2029
01:29:10.804 --> 01:29:11.805
Yes?

2030
01:29:14.599 --> 01:29:16.810
Yes.

2031
01:29:17.394 --> 01:29:18.728
Yeah.

2032
01:29:18.812 --> 01:29:19.813
You bet.

2033
01:29:20.605 --> 01:29:21.648
You bet.

2034
01:29:24.693 --> 01:29:28.321
[exhales]

2035
01:29:30.407 --> 01:29:31.992
But what I have...

